      "title": "Docker Handbook Cover",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Docker Handbook Cover",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Images and Builds",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Image== = read-only layers; ==container== = image + writable layer",
                "State goes in a volume: `-v data:/var/lib/db`",
                "Layers cache until an earlier one changes: ==deps before source==",
                "==Multi-stage==: only the last stage ships",
                "Pin the tag: `node:22-alpine`, not `:latest`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "dockerfile",
              "lines": [
                "FROM node:22 AS build",
                "WORKDIR /app",
                "COPY package*.json ./",
                "RUN npm ci",
                "COPY . .",
                "RUN npm run build",
                "FROM node:22-alpine",
                "COPY --from=build /app/dist ./dist"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Run It Right",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "starting",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "healthy",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unhealthy",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==One process== per container; logs to stdout",
                "`HEALTHCHECK CMD wget -qO- localhost:3000/health || exit 1`",
                "Config at runtime: `-e KEY=val` or `--env-file .env`",
                "Run as non-root: `USER app`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Compose",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "services:",
                "  web:",
                "    build: .",
                "    depends_on: {db: {condition: service_healthy}}",
                "  db:",
                "    image: postgres:16",
                "    environment: {POSTGRES_PASSWORD: example}",
                "    healthcheck: {test: [CMD, pg_isready]}"
              ],
              "note": "web reaches the database at db:5432"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never bake in",
              "text": "No secrets in ==ENV==, ARG or layers. Plain `depends_on` only waits for container start."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Images vs Containers",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Images vs Containers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Image vs Container",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Image",
                "Container"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Is",
                  "==read-only==, layered, immutable template",
                  "running or stopped instance"
                ],
                [
                  "Writable?",
                  "no",
                  "thin ==writable layer== on top"
                ],
                [
                  "Analogy",
                  "class / recipe",
                  "object / instance"
                ],
                [
                  "Count",
                  "one image",
                  "{green:many} containers from it"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Not a VM",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A container is an isolated ==process==",
                "{blue:Namespaces}: isolation",
                "{purple:cgroups}: CPU and memory limits",
                "Shares the ==host kernel==; a VM boots its own"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Start a container from `nginx:1.27`, host ==8080== to container ==80=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "docker run -d --name web -p 8080:80 nginx:1.27"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Data in the writable layer is ==lost on docker rm==. Keep state in a volume: `-v data:/var/lib/db`."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Container vs VM?** It shares the host kernel; no guest OS.",
                "**Data after docker rm?** Gone, unless it is in a volume."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Dockerfiles and Multi-Stage Builds",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Dockerfiles and Multi-Stage Builds",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Layers and Cache",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`RUN`, `COPY` and `ADD` each make a ==layer==",
                "Layers are cached; a change {red:rebuilds} every layer after it",
                "Copy `package.json` and install first, then `COPY` the source"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. CMD vs ENTRYPOINT",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "CMD",
                "ENTRYPOINT"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Role",
                  "default command",
                  "fixed executable"
                ],
                [
                  "Override",
                  "`docker run img cmd`",
                  "`--entrypoint`"
                ],
                [
                  "Example",
                  "`CMD [\"app.js\"]`",
                  "`ENTRYPOINT [\"node\"]`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Together, `CMD` is the default args: runs `node app.js`",
                "Use ==exec form== `[\"node\",\"app.js\"]` so signals reach the process"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Multi-Stage Builds",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Build stage",
                    "sub": "node:22 AS build",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "COPY --from=build",
                    "sub": "/app/dist only",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Final stage",
                    "sub": "node:22-alpine, ships; no compilers or dev deps",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "dockerfile",
              "lines": [
                "FROM node:22 AS build",
                "WORKDIR /app",
                "COPY package*.json ./",
                "RUN npm ci",
                "COPY . .",
                "RUN npm run build",
                "FROM node:22-alpine",
                "COPY --from=build /app/dist ./dist"
              ],
              "note": "assumes dist is bundled, no runtime packages"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`COPY . .` before install: every edit reinstalls",
                "No `.dockerignore`: `node_modules`, `.git`, `.env` enter the build context",
                "Secrets baked into layers stay in the image history"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Small Images and One Process Per Container",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Small Images and One Process Per Container",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Small Base Images",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Smaller image = ==faster pull== and smaller **attack surface**",
                "Pin an explicit tag: `node:22-alpine`, never `:latest`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Base",
                "Size",
                "Note"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Full Debian",
                  "~900MB+",
                  "everything included"
                ],
                [
                  "`-slim`",
                  "~200MB",
                  "trimmed Debian"
                ],
                [
                  "`node:22-alpine`",
                  "~160MB on disk",
                  "musl libc can break native deps"
                ],
                [
                  "distroless",
                  "smallest",
                  "no shell, no package manager"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. One Process Per Container",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One job each: ==web==, ==worker==, ==db==",
                "Scales, restarts and logs independently",
                "Write logs to ==stdout/stderr==",
                "Run as a **non-root** user:"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "dockerfile",
              "lines": [
                "RUN adduser -D app",
                "USER app"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Running `sshd` or several services via a supervisor",
                "Installing debug tools and caches in the final image"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Pinned small tag, ==one job== per container, ==non-root== user."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Health Checks and Environment Configuration",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Health Checks and Environment Configuration",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Health checks",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "dockerfile",
              "lines": [
                "HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s \\",
                "  --retries=3 --start-period=20s \\",
                "  CMD wget -qO- http://localhost:3000/health || exit 1"
              ],
              "note": "non-zero exit counts as a failed probe"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "starting",
                    "sub": "in start period",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "healthy",
                    "sub": "probe passes",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "x",
                    "text": "unhealthy",
                    "sub": "retries failed",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Tests that the ==app works==, not just that the process is alive",
                "A running container can still be {red:unhealthy}",
                "`docker ps` shows the status"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Configuration",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Twelve-factor: the ==same image== runs everywhere",
                "Settings are injected at ==runtime=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "When",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`ENV`",
                  "image default",
                  "safe defaults"
                ],
                [
                  "`ARG`",
                  "build time only",
                  "build options"
                ],
                [
                  "`-e KEY=val`",
                  "runtime",
                  "one setting"
                ],
                [
                  "`--env-file .env`",
                  "runtime",
                  "per environment"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Baking environment config or secrets into the image",
                "Committing `.env`",
                "No start period: slow apps marked unhealthy"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No secrets",
              "text": "Never put secrets in `ENV` or `ARG`. Use ==runtime secrets=="
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Docker Compose and Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Docker Compose and Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. compose.yaml",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Service keys: ==image== or ==build==, `ports`, `environment`, `volumes`, `depends_on`",
                "Default shared network: reach services by name, e.g. `db:5432`",
                "Plain `depends_on` waits for container {red:start} only",
                "`service_healthy` waits for the {green:health check}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "services:",
                "  web:",
                "    build: .",
                "    depends_on: {db: {condition: service_healthy}}",
                "  db:",
                "    image: postgres:16",
                "    environment: {POSTGRES_PASSWORD: example}",
                "    healthcheck: {test: [\"CMD-SHELL\",\"pg_isready -U postgres\"], interval: 5s, retries: 5}"
              ],
              "note": "the dependency needs its own healthcheck"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Stack commands",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`docker compose up -d --build`",
                  "start stack"
                ],
                [
                  "`docker compose down`",
                  "stop and remove"
                ],
                [
                  "`docker compose down -v`",
                  "also delete volumes"
                ],
                [
                  "`docker compose logs -f web`",
                  "follow logs"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Everyday commands",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`docker build -t app:1.0 .`",
                  "build image"
                ],
                [
                  "`docker ps -a` / `docker images`",
                  "list containers / images"
                ],
                [
                  "`docker logs -f c`",
                  "follow logs"
                ],
                [
                  "`docker exec -it c sh`",
                  "shell inside"
                ],
                [
                  "`docker stop c` / `docker rm c`",
                  "stop / remove"
                ],
                [
                  "`docker system prune`",
                  "clean unused"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Quick rules",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pin tags",
                "Order layers by change frequency",
                "Multi-stage for small images",
                "Non-root user",
                "One process per container",
                "Config via env",
                "Named volumes for state"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A Dockerfile runs `COPY . .` and then `RUN npm ci`. You change one line of source. What happens on rebuild?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The `COPY` layer changed, so `npm ci` reruns and reinstalls everything.",
                "Fix: copy `package*.json`, run `npm ci`, then `COPY . .`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Compose has `web` with plain `depends_on: [db]`. Why can `web` still fail to connect at startup?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Plain `depends_on` waits only for the db container to start, not to be ready.",
                "Add a db healthcheck and use `condition: service_healthy`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An app writes files to `/data` inside a container. You run `docker rm` and then `docker run` again. Are the files there?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No. They lived in the old container's writable layer, which `docker rm` deleted.",
                "Mount a named volume, such as `-v data:/data`, for state."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
